Hm... I think to do this without any hacks, we would need to move AsyncTaskCache into each respective Cache implementation.

Since the RemoteCache has no knowledge about whether the cacheProtocol is a combined Disk and Remote cache or just a single remote cache, we would have to unconditionally populate the AsyncTaskCache with a null value...

Something like (naming tbd):
```
ListenableFuture<Void> cacheUpload(context, digest, func, force) {
  switch context.getWriteCachePolicy() {
    case REMOTE_CACHE_ONLY:
      casUploadCache.execute(digest + "_REMOTE",
            RxFutures.toCompletable(
                () -> func(), directExecutor()),
            force);
     case DISK_CACHE_ONLY:
      return casUploadCache.execute(digest + "_DISK",
            RxFutures.toCompletable(
                () -> func(), directExecutor()),
            force);

     case ANY_CACHE:
      casUploadCache.execute(digest + "_DISK",
            RxFutures.toCompletable(
                () -> {}),
            force);
      return casUploadCache.execute(digest + "_REMOTE",
            RxFutures.toCompletable(
                () -> func(), directExecutor()),
            force);
  }
}
```

